From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: fan53555: accept the STI8070A on the Silergy path

The Anbernic RG DS Plus fits an STI8070A as vdd_cpu. It is register
compatible with the Silergy SYR82x, and Anbernic's own device tree drives
it as "silergy,syr827", but it reports die ID 13, so the Silergy setup
rejects it, vdd_cpu never registers and cpufreq-dt defers forever.

Use the SYR82x voltage table for it, which is what the vendor device tree
assumes (regulator-min-microvolt = 712500).
---
 drivers/regulator/fan53555.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c b/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c
--- a/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/fan53555.c
@@ -118,6 +118,7 @@
 enum {
 	SILERGY_SYR82X = 8,
 	SILERGY_SYR83X = 9,
+	SILERGY_STI8070A = 13,
 };
 
 struct fan53555_device_info {
@@ -395,6 +396,7 @@
 	switch (di->chip_id) {
 	case SILERGY_SYR82X:
 	case SILERGY_SYR83X:
+	case SILERGY_STI8070A:
 		di->vsel_min = 712500;
 		di->vsel_step = 12500;
 		break;
